  "term": "Symmetrel",
  "definition": "Symmetrel is a brand name for amantadine hydrochloride, a drug with antiviral and antiparkinsonian effects. In brain-related use, it is described as affecting dopamine activity and also having some influence on NMDA- and acetylcholine-related signaling.",
